---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'May 19, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Amplo Consulting"
  description="Terms governing your use of the Amplo Consulting website and related services."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="pt-32 md:pt-40 pb-24 md:pb-32">
    <div class="container-site max-w-3xl legal-doc">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[var(--color-gold)]">Terms</p>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,3.5rem)] leading-[1.08]">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p class="mt-10">
        These Terms of Service ("<strong>Terms</strong>") govern your
        access to and use of
        <a href="https://amploconsulting.com">amploconsulting.com</a>
        (the "<strong>Site</strong>") operated by Amplo Consulting, LLC
        ("<strong>Amplo</strong>," "<strong>we</strong>,"
        "<strong>us</strong>," or "<strong>our</strong>"). By using the
        Site you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree,
        please do not use the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. No Attorney-Client or Consulting Relationship</h2>
      <p>
        The Site provides general information about Amplo and the
        services we offer. Reviewing the Site, contacting us through the
        Site, or sending us information through the contact form
        <strong>does not create an attorney-client relationship,
        consulting engagement, fiduciary duty, or any other professional
        relationship</strong> between you and Amplo. A professional
        relationship with Amplo arises only when both parties sign a
        written engagement agreement that expressly creates it. Until
        such an agreement is signed, do not send us confidential or
        privileged information.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Not Legal Advice</h2>
      <p>
        Content on the Site is provided for general informational
        purposes only and does not constitute legal, regulatory, tax, or
        business advice. Laws and regulations change frequently and vary
        by jurisdiction and circumstance. You should consult qualified
        counsel about your particular situation before acting on any
        information you find on the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Use of the Site</h2>
      <p>You agree that you will not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>use the Site for any unlawful purpose or in violation of these Terms;</li>
        <li>attempt to interfere with, disrupt, or gain unauthorized access to the Site, its infrastructure, or any user account;</li>
        <li>submit information through the Site that is false, misleading, infringing, defamatory, or unlawful;</li>
        <li>copy, reproduce, distribute, or create derivative works of any content on the Site except as expressly permitted by these Terms; or</li>
        <li>use any automated means, including bots or scrapers, to access the Site in a manner that imposes an unreasonable load on our infrastructure.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        The Site, including its text, design, layout, graphics, logos,
        and other content, is the property of Amplo or its licensors and
        is protected by United States and international intellectual
        property laws. You may view and print pages of the Site for your
        own personal, non-commercial reference. Any other use requires
        our prior written consent.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Submissions Through the Contact Form</h2>
      <p>
        Information you submit through the contact form will be handled
        as described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. By
        submitting information, you represent that it is accurate, that
        you have the right to share it, and that doing so will not
        violate any law or any obligation you owe to a third party.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-Party Links and Services</h2>
      <p>
        The Site may contain links to third-party websites or rely on
        third-party services (such as Google, Resend, and Vercel) to
        operate. We do not control those websites or services and we are
        not responsible for their content, policies, or practices.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The Site is provided on an "<strong>as is</strong>" and
        "<strong>as available</strong>" basis. To the fullest extent
        permitted by law, Amplo disclaims all warranties of any kind,
        whether express or implied, including warranties of
        merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
        non-infringement, accuracy, and uninterrupted operation. We do
        not warrant that the Site will be error-free, secure, or
        continuously available.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Amplo and its members,
        managers, employees, contractors, and agents will not be liable
        for any indirect, incidental, consequential, special, exemplary,
        or punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, revenue, data,
        or goodwill, arising out of or related to your use of the Site,
        even if we have been advised of the possibility of such damages.
        In no event will our aggregate liability arising out of or
        related to the Site exceed one hundred U.S. dollars (US$100.00).
      </p>

      <h2>9. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless Amplo and its
        members, managers, employees, contractors, and agents from and
        against any claims, damages, losses, liabilities, and expenses
        (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or related
        to your use of the Site, your violation of these Terms, or your
        violation of any rights of a third party.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Governing Law and Venue</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida,
        without regard to its conflict-of-laws principles. Any dispute
        arising out of or related to these Terms or the Site will be
        resolved exclusively in the state or federal courts located in
        Miami-Dade County, Florida, and you consent to the personal
        jurisdiction of those courts.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may revise these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will
        update the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of the Site
        after a revision constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms? Contact us at
        <a href="mailto:info@amploconsulting.com">info@amploconsulting.com</a>
        or by mail at:
      </p>
      <p>
        Amplo Consulting, LLC<br />
        Miami, Florida<br />
        United States
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
